engine: final bang over as question plus baseline lift

The intonation rules test for question records and never for bang,
so a final bang took declarative defaults and read flat. Until the
rules learn the mark, a final bang is handed over as a question mark:
same phones, working rise, with a higher baseline lift than a real
question. Mid-sentence bangs keep their bytes. All languages shout.
Applied at build time so CI builds the same tree.
diff --git a/src/eci/synth/eci_synthtext.c b/src/eci/synth/eci_synthtext.c
index fb97f8e..d5ccd75 100644
--- a/src/eci/synth/eci_synthtext.c
+++ b/src/eci/synth/eci_synthtext.c
@@ -339,6 +339,69 @@ static int utf8ToWestern(const char *text, uint32_t len, char *out,
